CloudBurrow patch 15 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1089); needs patch 0004.

The bug: patch 0004 keeps a FLOAT64 NaN as the value envelope, a TEXT
value, where every other FLOAT64 is a REAL, and SQLite sorts TEXT after
every REAL; so ORDER BY put NaN after +inf. In an aggregate's ORDER BY
(ARRAY_AGG(x ORDER BY x)) NaN < x is false both ways, so it sorted last
too. BigQuery sorts NULL, then NaN, then -inf ... +inf
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-types#floating_point_semantics).

The patch orders a FLOAT64 ORDER BY column first by whether it is NULL, a
NaN (TEXT) or a number, and has the aggregate sort put a NaN before every
other non-NULL value. Comparisons (NaN = NaN is FALSE), MIN and MAX (NaN
when any input is NaN), GROUP BY and DISTINCT already agreed with
BigQuery. Window ORDER BY is not changed. nan_order_test.go fails without
the patch.

